{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-q4.10.1:000021:note_appended:bob-cli-q4.10.1.1:2495feab9468c85580aea2cec5f4a58142fd9aff97f7ecdaf55a15c64f0bebd6","timestamp":"2026-11-25T19:54:22Z","actor":"bob-cli-q4.10.1.1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-q4.10.1.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Settle-bridge landed in bob-navigation-hotkeys 2.107.6 (deployed, no -F). Guarded consumer of ledger-tools taskSettle v1: applyNavSettledEditorWrite / AnnotatedWrite / RestoreWrite / prepareNavSettledFilePostimage. Missing/old/throwing provider falls back to the existing gesture; stale preimage and A-to-B path/view refuse without writing; restore never settles. applyEditorContentTransaction is not an unconditional settle hook.\n\nFLUSH ROUTES\n- commands: onload installNavTaskSettleCommandFlush wraps registered bob-navigation-hotkeys:* callback/editorCallback; checkCallback/editorCheckCallback only when checking !== true (docs-inventory forbids aliasing addCommand, so wrapping is registry-based like ledger-tools)\n- vim: registerVimMappings defineAction wrappers for toggle pin, jump back, jump forward\n- physical (after chord/mode, before count/cursor): handleOpenTaskJumpPhysicalKeydown, handleCountedBulletPropertyPhysicalKeydown, handleCountedLaneTogglePhysicalKeydown, handleCountedTransclusionTogglePhysicalKeydown, handleCountedTaskMovePhysicalKeydown, handleReviewRefreshPhysicalKeydown, handleTaskSplitPhysicalKeydown, handlePomodoroSplitPhysicalKeydown\n- publicApi: reviewWalk.capture, claimReviewWalkCompletion, openDependencyStage, removeDependency, openFileInActiveLeaf\n- skipped: checkCallback when checking === true; arbitrary typing / every keydown; recordJump; review-refresh held-key tracking at start of handleReviewRefreshPhysicalKeydown\n\nIdentity: unique blockId is authoritative; disappeared/duplicate IDs do not fall back to a stale line number. Queue/resume/jump maps compose with settle lineMap. Cursor stay records one jump.\n\nVerified: npm test (9572 pass / 4 skip / 0 fail + 26 perf); 22 new adapter/command/identity tests including real taskSettle v1 AREA fixture."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-q4.10.1:000022:note_appended:bob-cli-q4.10.1.1:cf7d8bc1836b38a163b24a76bc8d6ca5a6e30d229b7bce358d48e92fb9057ee1","timestamp":"2026-11-25T19:56:20Z","actor":"bob-cli-q4.10.1.1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-q4.10.1.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"settle-bridge landed in bob-navigation-hotkeys 2.107.6 (deployed without -F). Guarded taskSettle v1 consumer: applyNavSettledEditorWrite/AnnotatedWrite/RestoreWrite and prepareNavSettledFilePostimage; missing/old/throwing provider keeps the existing gesture; stale preimage and A-to-B path/view refuse; restore writes exact recorded bytes. applyEditorContentTransaction is not an unconditional settle hook. Command flush wraps registered bob-navigation-hotkeys:* callbacks at end of onload (docs-inventory forbids addCommand alias); Vim defineAction wrappers; physical routes flush after chord/mode before count/cursor; public APIs flush on capture/claim/openDependency/removeDependency/openFileInActiveLeaf. Identity: unique blockId is authoritative; disappeared/duplicate IDs do not fall back to a stale line. npm test: 9572 pass / 4 skip / 0 fail + 26 perf; 22 new adapter/command/identity tests. No leftover --epic-symbol entries."}}
